Charge on Conducting balls <img src="assets/opbp-3cd96f2e998e/balls.png" alt="原题配图">

Five identical neutral conducting balls hanging from strings are numbered 1 to 5. As shown in the Figure above. Balls 1 and 2 touch as they are brought near a highly charged metal sphere and then are separated, with ball 1 closer to the sphere. Ball 3 contacts both the metal sphere and ball 4. Ball 4 is pulled away from ball 3, and then ball 3 is pulled away from the metal sphere.

## Part 1

Following these charging steps, what is the sign of the charge on ball 1?

### 作答区（非答案）
- negative \text{[参数缺失]}
- positive \text{[参数缺失]}
- Zero \text{[参数缺失]}

## Part 2

Following these charging steps, what is the sign of the charge on ball 3?

### 作答区（非答案）
- Negative \text{[参数缺失]}
- Positive \text{[参数缺失]}
- Zero \text{[参数缺失]}

## Part 3

Following these charging steps, ball 1 is attracted to (choose the best answer):

### 作答区（非答案）
- Ball 2 only \text{[参数缺失]}
- Ball 5 only \text{[参数缺失]}
- None of the balls \text{[参数缺失]}
- All of the other balls (2, 3, 4 and 5) \text{[参数缺失]}
- Balls 2, 3 and 4 only \text{[参数缺失]}

